    "title": "Man arrested after hours-long Madison County standoff - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Dustin Massengill ,\n2 hours ago\nRICHMOND, Ky. ( FOX 56 ) — A man has been arrested after a standoff with authorities in Madison County.\nThe Madison County Sheriff’s Office said dispatchers were called around 3:28 p.m. Tuesday about a man with a handgun making threats behind a home on Brassfield Road.\nLATEST KENTUCKY NEWS: According to the sheriff’s office, when deputies arrived, they found Joshua Botkin with a handgun.\nThe sheriff’s office said that after several hours of negotiating, Botkin surrendered to deputies and was taken into custody.\nBotkin was reportedly arrested and charged with second-degree arson in connection with a separate incident earlier that day and was booked into the Madison County Detention Center.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to FOX 56 News.",
